{"_createdAt":"2026-09-20T03:45:58Z","_id":"paper-choba-2025","_rev":"fBrCjNug36o8mO87SwSxoa","_type":"surveyPaper","_updatedAt":"2026-09-20T03:45:58Z","authors":["Oghonyon, R.","Nnurum, E.U.","Oguejiofor, C.V."],"citation":"Oghonyon, R., Nnurum, E.U., Oguejiofor, C.V. (2025). Evaluation of Resistivity Data for Delineating Potential Potable Water Accumulation Zone at Choba, Rivers State Nigeria. International Journal of Research and Scientific Innovation (IJRSI), XII(VII), 1525-1532.","doi":"https://doi.org/10.51244/IJRSI.2025.120700155","journal":"International Journal of Research and Scientific Innovation (IJRSI)","license":"unmarked","sourceNotes":"Table 5 transcribed directly. Cumulative-depth arithmetic checked and reconciles cleanly for all 4 finite layers (unlike Bori/Etche, no inconsistency found here).\n\nCurve-type note: Paper's own text (Discussion) states the trend as ℓ1<ℓ2>ℓ3<ℓ4<ℓ5 - NOT monotonic (real dip at layer 3) - yet the paper still calls it an 'A-type curve' throughout. This is the THIRD confirmed instance (after Etche's Odufor and Opiro) of this research community using 'A-type' as a loose descriptor for 'broadly increasing with depth' rather than the strict monotonic definition. Our classifier correctly declines to assert a specific type here (5 layers, non-monotonic -> 'unclassified' per interpret_layers.py's calibrated rule) rather than parroting the paper's looser label.","title":"Evaluation of Resistivity Data for Delineating Potential Potable Water Accumulation Zone at Choba, Rivers State Nigeria","year":2025}
{"_createdAt":"2026-09-20T03:45:58Z","_id":"paper-etche-2022","_rev":"fBrCjNug36o8mO87SwSxoa","_type":"surveyPaper","_updatedAt":"2026-09-20T03:45:58Z","authors":["Nwankwoala, H.O.","Osayande, A.D.","Nwosu, C.H.","Ugwu, S.A."],"citation":"Nwankwoala, H.O., Osayande, A.D., Nwosu, C.H., Ugwu, S.A. (2022). Groundwater exploration using vertical electrical sounding techniques in parts of Etche Local Government Area of Rivers State, Nigeria. Global Journal of Engineering and Technology Advances, 11(01), 088-100.","doi":"https://doi.org/10.30574/gjeta.2022.11.1.0070","journal":"Global Journal of Engineering and Technology Advances","license":"cc-by-4.0","sourceNotes":"Values transcribed directly from the paper's Tables 1-8 (per-station IPI2/ID Interpex-inverted layer results) and Table 9 (curve type summary).\n\nKnown source inconsistency: Checked cumulative-depth arithmetic (depth[i] should equal depth[i-1] + thickness[i]) for every station. It holds for Opiro, Odufor, and layers 1-4 of Ndashi/Umuokom. It does NOT hold for: Egwi layer 4 depth (printed 37.25, arithmetic gives 44.25), Ulakwo layers 2-3 depths, Okehi layer 3 depth, Akpoku layer 2 depth, and the LAST layer's depth specifically for Ndashi and Umuokom (both off by roughly the same ~9-10m, suggesting a systematic issue in the source paper's table typesetting, not a one-off typo). Transcribed exactly as printed regardless - not silently corrected, since guessing at the 'right' number would be fabrication, not transcription.","title":"Groundwater exploration using vertical electrical sounding techniques in parts of Etche Local Government Area of Rivers State, Nigeria","year":2022}
{"_createdAt":"2026-09-20T03:45:58Z","_id":"paper-bori-2024","_rev":"jLe7hSgM7sILxxhuYoAWA5","_type":"surveyPaper","_updatedAt":"2026-09-20T03:51:29Z","authors":["Menegbo, B.G.","Davies, O.A.","Horsfall, O.I."],"citation":"Menegbo, B.G., Davies, O.A., Horsfall, O.I. (2024). Assessment of Aquifer Resistivity, Depth, and Thickness using Vertical Electrical Sounding (VES) in Parts of Bori Metropolis for Groundwater Exploration. World Journal of Advanced Research and Reviews, 24(02), 275-285.","doi":"https://doi.org/10.30574/wjarr.2024.24.2.3293","journal":"World Journal of Advanced Research and Reviews","license":"cc-by-4.0","sourceNotes":"Verified directly against the source PDF (wjarr.com/sites/default/files/fulltext_pdf/WJARR-2024-3293.pdf). The paper's own p.7 Table 1 (summary table) prints swapped station-name labels for two rows: the row labeled 'BMGS bori field' actually carries Kenpoly sec school field's coordinates and Figure-2-panel-(b) values (3706 ohm-m), while the row labeled 'Kenpoly sec school field' carries BMGS bori field's coordinates and Figure-2-panel-(c) values (2950 ohm-m). This is checkable against the paper's own p.3 coordinate table and its own Figure 2 captions, which agree with each other and disagree with the p.7 table's row labels. Both versions are recorded in this Knowledge Base as separate readings per station, tagged by which part of the paper they came from.","title":"Assessment of Aquifer Resistivity, Depth, and Thickness using Vertical Electrical Sounding (VES) in Parts of Bori Metropolis for Groundwater Exploration","year":2024}
