{"_createdAt":"2026-09-20T03:45:58Z","_id":"reading-choba-choba-lawntennisfield","_rev":"iS10sBQXwjmqz8At2Q0l0e","_type":"vesReading","_updatedAt":"2026-09-20T04:22:20Z","aquiferLithology":"gravel (layer 4, 474.3 ohm-m) / conglomerate (layer 5, 597.1 ohm-m, discontinuous)","curveTypePublished":"A","layers":[{"_key":"l0","_type":"layer","cumulativeDepthM":2.535,"layerIndex":1,"resistivityOhmM":91.2,"thicknessM":2.535},{"_key":"l1","_type":"layer","cumulativeDepthM":18.37,"layerIndex":2,"resistivityOhmM":380.2,"thicknessM":15.83},{"_key":"l2","_type":"layer","cumulativeDepthM":38.73,"layerIndex":3,"resistivityOhmM":43.25,"thicknessM":20.36},{"_key":"l3","_type":"layer","cumulativeDepthM":71.78,"layerIndex":4,"resistivityOhmM":474.3,"thicknessM":33.05},{"_key":"l4","_type":"layer","cumulativeDepthM":null,"layerIndex":5,"resistivityOhmM":597.1,"thicknessM":null}],"paper":{"_ref":"paper-choba-2025","_type":"reference"},"reportedAquiferDepthM":71.78,"reportedAquiferResistivityOhmM":474.3,"reportedAquiferThicknessM":33.05,"site":{"_ref":"site-choba","_type":"reference"},"sourceLocation":"Table 5 (values), Discussion and Conclusion sections (aquifer designation)","station":"Choba-LawnTennisField","transcriptionNote":"Verified against the source PDF. The paper genuinely holds two different answers for 'the aquifer' here, not one: layer 5 (597.1 ohm-m, ~90m estimated depth) is called its highest-resistivity 'potential quality aquifer zone' in the Discussion, but the same Discussion section's actual actionable recommendation is 'advisable to cite a borehole at layer 4 (474.3ohm-m)' -- specifically because layer 5 is discontinuous (not reliably present across the site) while layer 4 is not. This reading uses layer 4 as reportedAquiferResistivityOhmM because that is the paper's own siting recommendation, but layer 5's value is preserved in the layers array and should not be discarded -- both are real signals from the same paper for different reasons.\n\nSeparately, curve-type note: the paper's own Discussion states the resistivity trend as l1<l2>l3<l4<l5 (a real dip at layer 3, non-monotonic), yet the same Discussion explicitly calls it an 'A-type curve pattern, defined by progressive increase in resistivity with depth' -- the paper's own label contradicts its own stated trend."}
